      <section class="page-hero" style="background-image:url('assets/img/dest-guilin.jpg');"><div class="container"><span class="breadcrumb"><a href="index.html">Home</a> &nbsp;/&nbsp; <a href="tours.html">Destinations</a> &nbsp;/&nbsp; Guilin</span><h1>Guilin <span class="zh" style="font-family:var(--font-zh);font-size:0.65em;color:var(--gold);">桂林</span></h1><p>Guilin and Yangshuo are the China of scroll paintings — karst peaks rising like jade fingers from emerald rivers, fishermen on bamboo rafts, and rice paddies cascading down hillsides.</p></div></section>
  - label: "Why visit Guilin?"
    html: |
      <section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="split"><div class="split-media reveal"><img src="assets/img/dest-guilin.jpg" alt="Guilin" /><div class="seal-stamp" aria-hidden="true">桂<br/>林</div></div><div class="split-copy reveal reveal-d1"><span class="eyebrow">Rivers & Karsts</span><h2 class="display-h2">Why visit Guilin?</h2><p>Guilin and Yangshuo are the China of scroll paintings — karst peaks rising like jade fingers from emerald rivers, fishermen on bamboo rafts, and rice paddies cascading down hillsides. This is the landscape that has inspired Chinese poets and painters for more than a thousand years.</p><p>It is also the most relaxing corner of China to travel: slow boat rides, easy cycle paths, and riverside guesthouses where the only alarm clock is a water buffalo. Few places let you unhook from the world so completely.</p></div></div></div></section>
