  - label: "Iconic experiences in Guilin"
    html: |
      <section class="section" style="background:var(--white);"><div class="container"><div class="section-head reveal"><span class="eyebrow centered">Must-See Sights</span><h2 class="display-h2">Iconic experiences in Guilin</h2></div><div class="feature-grid" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);"><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>Li River Cruise</h3><p>The 83 km cruise from Guilin to Yangshuo is one of the world's great boat journeys — misty peaks, water buffalo and cormorant fishermen drift past.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>Yangshuo Countryside</h3><p>Cycle through karst valleys, bamboo groves and tiny villages. Stop for lunch at a farmhouse and swim in the Yulong River.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>Longji Rice Terraces</h3><p>The Dragon's Backbone terraces carved into the mountains over 650 years. Hike between Zhuang and Yao minority villages.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>Reed Flute Cave</h3><p>A vast limestone cave of multicoloured stalactites lit like a natural cathedral — a cool, otherworldly half-day.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>Elephant Trunk Hill</h3><p>Guilin's emblem — a karst hill whose arch perfectly mimics a trunk drinking from the Li River.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>Xingping Town</h3><p>The postcard cove printed on the 20-yuan note — misted peaks and a quiet old town worth an afternoon.</p></div></div></div></section>
  - label: "Taste of Guangxi"
    html: |
      <section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="split"><div class="split-copy reveal"><span class="eyebrow">Food Capital</span><h2 class="display-h2">Taste of Guangxi</h2><p>Guilin's cooking is fresh, river-led and gently sour — a world away from the chillies of the west. The signature is beer fish (pijiu yu), river fish braised with beer, tomatoes and green peppers. Our guides lead you to the noodle stalls and riverside kitchens that locals love.</p><p>We tailor every meal to the season — cool river snails in summer, hearty clay-pot fish when the mist rolls in.</p><ul class="tour-highlights" style="grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:10px;"><li><strong>Beer fish (pijiu yu)</strong> — Yangshuo's river-fish speciality braised with beer and tomato</li><li><strong>Guilin rice noodles (mifen)</strong> — a fragrant breakfast staple with pickles</li><li><strong>Oil tea (you cha)</strong> — a savoury tea with rice, peanuts and herbs, a minority staple</li><li><strong>Stuffed river snails</strong> — a beloved local snack</li><li><strong>Luosifen</strong> — the famous fermented rice-noodle soup (an acquired, addictive taste)</li></ul></div><div class="split-media reveal reveal-d1"><img src="assets/img/guilin-food.jpg" alt="Guilin beer fish" /><div class="seal-stamp" aria-hidden="true">桂<br/>味</div></div></div></div></section>
  - label: "A perfect 4-day journey"
    html: |
      <section class="section" style="background:var(--paper-deep);"><div class="container"><div class="section-head reveal"><span class="eyebrow centered">Sample Itinerary</span><h2 class="display-h2">A perfect 4-day journey</h2><p>Every journey we design is tailor-made — this is a favourite starting point.</p></div><div class="steps-grid" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:22px;"><div class="step reveal"><span class="step-num">01</span><h3>Arrival &amp; City Lights</h3><p>Private transfer, Elephant Trunk Hill at golden hour, then the Two Rivers & Four Lakes light cruise after dark.</p></div><div class="step reveal reveal-d1"><span class="step-num">02</span><h3>Li River to Yangshuo</h3><p>The 83 km Li River cruise to Yangshuo, an afternoon on West Street, and the open-air Impression Sanjie Liu show.</p></div><div class="step reveal reveal-d2"><span class="step-num">03</span><h3>Countryside &amp; River</h3><p>A bamboo raft on the jade Yulong River, easy cycling through karst valleys, and a farmhouse lunch with a cooking class.</p></div><div class="step reveal reveal-d3"><span class="step-num">04</span><h3>Terraces Farewell</h3><p>Private drive to the Longji rice terraces, a hike between Zhuang and Yao villages, then transfer to Guilin for your flight.</p></div></div></div></section>
  - label: "Guilin after dark"
    html: |
      <section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="split"><div class="split-media reveal"><img src="assets/img/guilin-night.jpg" alt="Yangshuo and Li River at night" /></div><div class="split-copy reveal reveal-d1"><span class="eyebrow">Night Views</span><h2 class="display-h2">Guilin after dark</h2><p>Guilin and Yangshuo are magical after sunset. Karst peaks turn to silhouette under the moon, and the Li River mirrors a string of lanterns. Yangshuo's West Street buzzes with travellers, while the colossal Impression show stages opera on the water itself.</p><ul class="tour-highlights" style="grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:10px;"><li>Impression Sanjie Liu — a vast open-air show staged on the Li River</li><li>Yangshuo West Street — bars, live music and street food till late</li><li>Yulong River lantern raft under the stars</li><li>Guilin Two Rivers & Four Lakes light cruise</li></ul></div></div></div></section>
  - label: "Beyond the city"
    html: |
      <section class="section" style="background:var(--white);"><div class="container"><div class="section-head reveal"><span class="eyebrow centered">Nearby Escapes</span><h2 class="display-h2">Beyond the city</h2></div><div class="feature-grid" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);"><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>Sanjiang Dong Villages</h3><p>Wind-Rain bridges and drum towers of the Dong minority — a living woodcraft tradition 3 h away. Overnight in a stilted guesthouse.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M3 18l6-8 4 5 3-4 5 7z"/><path d="M3 21h18"/></svg></div><h3>Detian Waterfall</h3><p>Asia's largest transnational waterfall, on the Vietnam border, plunging in tiered curtains through green gorges. A scenic drive.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M4 18h16M6 18V8l6-4 6 4v10"/><path d="M10 18v-4h4v4"/></svg></div><h3>Huangyao Ancient Town</h3><p>A beautifully preserved Ming-era town of stone lanes and banyan trees — far quieter than the headline sights.</p></div></div></div></section>
  - label: "Good to know"
    html: |
      <section class="commit-band section"><div class="container"><div class="section-head reveal" style="margin-bottom:20px;"><span class="eyebrow centered">Travel Tips</span><h2 class="display-h2">Good to know before you go</h2></div><div class="commit-grid" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;"><div class="commit-item reveal"><span class="commit-check">✓</span><div><strong>Best season</strong><p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.72);margin-top:6px;">Spring mist (April–May) and autumn's golden terraces (October) are the postcard windows. Summer is lush but humid.</p></div></div><div class="commit-item reveal"><span class="commit-check">✓</span><div><strong>River cruises</strong><p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.72);margin-top:6px;">We book upper-deck seats and a morning departure for the best light and the fewest crowds on the Li River.</p></div></div><div class="commit-item reveal"><span class="commit-check">✓</span><div><strong>Cycling</strong><p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.72);margin-top:6px;">Yangshuo's paths are flat and easy; e-bikes and support vehicles are always on hand if you'd rather cruise.</p></div></div><div class="commit-item reveal"><span class="commit-check">✓</span><div><strong>Weather</strong><p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.72);margin-top:6px;">Humid subtropical — pack a light rain layer and quick-dry shoes; the mist that makes the photos is never far off.</p></div></div></div></div></section>
